{"answer":"None of the supplied papers directly address “Bekkers equivariant neural fields.”

Paper [1] discusses generalized reduction for flexible equivariant neural fields under group actions (reducing invariants on X × M to invariants of an isotropy subgroup), and [2] introduces an “Attentive Latent Fields (MetaLF)” model framed as an optimization encoder perspective for equivariant neural fields. However, the results do not mention Bekkers or specifically connect to any “Bekkers” formulation of equivariant neural fields.

Other papers cover related equivariance theory (e.g., groupoid-equivariant networks [3] and order/sheaf/category equivariant frameworks [6]) and equivariant applications in neural surrogates [8], but again none match the requested “Bekkers” topic.","grounded":false}
